BT 1 0 0 1 26 37.2 Tm (HOW TO CHECK INTO A NET) Tj T* ET
.070588 .137255 .231373 rg
n 262 34.2 230 11 re f*
1 1 1 rg
BT /F2 6.8 Tf 8.16 TL ET
BT 1 0 0 1 266 37.2 Tm (REPEATER ETIQUETTE & TROUBLESHOOTING) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 5.7 Tf 6.84 TL ET
.145098 .192157 .239216 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 26 25.2 Tm (1.  Listen first \227 wait for net control to call for check-ins.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 266 25.2 Tm (·  Pause after keying \227 repeaters take ~1/2 s to come up.) Tj T* ET
.145098 .192157 .239216 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 26 18.2 Tm (2.  Key up, pause 1/2 second \(let the repeater open\), then talk.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 266 18.2 Tm (·  Leave 2 s between overs so others can break in.) Tj T* ET
.145098 .192157 .239216 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 26 11.2 Tm (3.  Give:  call sign \(phonetically\) · first name · city.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 266 11.2 Tm (·  ID with your call sign every 10 min and at sign-off.) Tj T* ET
.145098 .192157 .239216 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 26 4.2 Tm (4.  Add \223no traffic\224 \227 or briefly state what you have.) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 266 4.2 Tm (·  Can\222t hear it?  Out of range, or it needs a receive tone.) Tj T* ET
